  "notes": "Same two-step at 174, opposite second kick: liquid steps to the and-of-3, jump-up hits straight on beat 3, and everything else follows from that squareness. Two to three ghost kicks and snares a bar at 30–40% fill the e and a slots, the snare is layered with a clap a few milliseconds late so it cracks rather than rolls, and the hook is not the melody — it is the bass. The riff is its own figure over an independent 16th grid, root/b3/4/5/b7/octave, portamento between the notes, sitting in the sine-sub octave under the kick. Harmony gets out of its way: a static i or an i–bII stab, triads, no jazz extensions.",
